      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When hunting a replacement, rank these factors:\n\n1. **Total travel time** – look for routes under 20 hours (typical one‑stop options are 16‑19 h).  \n2. **Number of connections** – a single layover is far less stressful than two or more.  \n3. **Layover length** – aim for 2‑4 h; anything shorter risks missing the next flight, anything longer adds unnecessary idle time.  \n4. **Departure window** – pick the earliest possible after your original time so you don’t lose more of your trip.  \n\nScan the airline’s “shortest‑duration” or “one‑stop only” filters, compare airlines for the same itinerary (e.g., LHR‑DXB‑SIN, LHR‑HKG‑SIN, LHR‑SIN direct if available), and book the option that meets the three criteria above while staying within your budget. Safe travels!",
