      "content": "Yes—keep these connection tips in mind:\n\n* **Same‑ticket itinerary** – If the flights are on one booking, the airline will re‑tag your bags and protect you if a delay causes a missed connection.  \n* **Minimum connection time (MCT)** – Verify that the layover meets the airport’s official MCT (usually 90 min in Dubai, 120 min in Hong Kong) to avoid tight transfers.  \n* **Transit‑visa requirements** – Some nationals need a visa even for a short layover in Dubai; check the airline or airport website before you book.  \n* **Terminal changes** – In both DXB and HKG, most international transfers stay within the same terminal, but verify the gate/terminal on your boarding pass so you don’t waste time walking between concourses.  \n\nFollowing these will help keep your bags and schedule on track. Safe journey!",
      "source": "target",
